    },
    {
      "ref": "01KGWG99",
      "text": "Define typed event data schemas per EventType — session.start, session.update (with tool_call/sessionUpdate variants), session.end, prompt.sent, tool.call, tool.result, note. Current z.unknown() data field makes it impossible to reliably query events without reverse-engineering from real JSONL files.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-07T16:52:11.891Z",
      "tags": [
        "reflection",
        "sessions",
        "schema"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KGWQ2T",
      "text": "Session log compaction: at end of each ralph loop, replace raw events.jsonl with a compiled stats file (event counts by type, tool usage frequency, duration, task transitions, error summary). Keep session folders and context snapshots intact but prune the raw log. This gives trend analysis capability without unbounded log growth. Could be a kspec session compact command or automatic post-loop step.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-07T18:51:00.259Z",
      "tags": [
        "deferred"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KGWZR7",
      "text": "Active context from meta: use the meta database (observations, conventions, patterns) as a dynamic context source that automatically surfaces relevant entries based on current activity. E.g. when reviewing plan-import code, auto-surface friction observations tagged with plan-import. When doing code review, pull in resolved friction patterns as review priors. Replaces manual markdown maintenance (AGENTS.md, skill docs) with structured data that stays current as observations accumulate. Could use conventions or a new meta item type for durable patterns distinct from one-off observations.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-07T21:22:29.717Z",
      "tags": [
        "reflection",
        "meta",
        "architecture"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KH20S1",
      "text": "Centralize daemon port default (3456) — currently hardcoded in 6 places: src/schema/spec.ts, src/cli/index.ts, src/cli/commands/serve.ts, packages/daemon/src/index.ts, packages/web-ui/src/lib/constants.ts, packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/test-base.ts. Extract to a shared constant to prevent drift.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-09T20:16:36.881Z",
      "tags": [
        "code-hygiene",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHA982",
      "text": "Formalize CLI usage analysis as a repeatable workflow. Tools exist in .claude-research/tools/ (parse-ralph-logs.mjs, parse-claude-logs.mjs, compile-data.mjs) plus interactive HTML report. Consider: kspec skill, CLI command, or standalone workflow. Re-run after implementing the 6 CLI agent-UX improvements to measure impact.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-13T01:18:34.385Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHCYW7",
      "text": "Add repeated-flag support to --status filter (ac-repeated-flag gap from PR #354). Commander.js .option() needs a collect function to accumulate repeated --status flags into an array. Currently only comma-separated works. Small fix: change .option('-s, --status <status>') to use Commander's variadic/collect pattern, then feed array into parseMultiStatus().",
      "created_at": "2026-02-14T02:15:03.519Z",
      "tags": [
