    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHJ4RV",
      "text": "Silent error swallowing in setup pipeline: multiple bare catch {} blocks in setup.ts lose diagnostic info. At minimum should log at debug/verbose level for troubleshooting.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T02:34:16.813Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHJ4RV",
      "text": "Legacy renderClaudeCodeSkill diverges from claudeCodeRenderer: uses old writeRenderHash (not platform-specific), lacks outputDir support, returns old type. setup.ts still uses it. Should route through registry and deprecate standalone function.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T02:34:16.835Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKTNJ",
      "text": "Codex and Claude Code renderers share ~70% duplicated render logic (content loading, frontmatter stripping, idempotency check, file writing, hash storage, dir copying). Extract shared base render function with hooks for platform-specific steps.\n\n---\n\nTriage 2026-02-22: 8/13 sub-items RESOLVED by PRs #408 #412 #403. Remaining: getSetupStatus staleness, skill update mutation, naming inconsistency, redundant defaults, deprecated_target reuse.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:16:11.540Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKTNJ",
      "text": "getSetupStatus always reports \"current\" if hash file exists, cannot detect staleness. Should load meta context and compare hash to detect when agents.md needs regeneration.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:16:11.605Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKTNJ",
      "text": "skill update mutates loaded skill objects in-place before saveMetaItem. If save fails partway, in-memory state diverges from disk. Should copy before mutation.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:16:11.623Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKTNJ",
      "text": "Naming inconsistency: isKspecManagedSkill (skill-render.ts) vs isKspecManaged (skill.ts) for same logic. Standardize to one name.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:16:11.644Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKTNJ",
      "text": "Redundant platform/tags/depends_on defaults in skill CLI — manually set before SkillSchema.safeParse which already applies them. Remove manual defaults.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:16:11.678Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKTNJ",
      "text": "deprecated_target warning type reused for skill-specific warnings (depends_on validation, orphaned dirs). Add proper skill warning types for better filtering.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:16:11.692Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHKVQG",
      "text": "Ralph loop consolidation pass: add a cleanup/consolidation iteration every N PRs or at loop end. The PR-by-PR review process misses cross-PR duplication accumulation — 32 PRs in last loop produced 24 inbox items of tech debt. A periodic consolidation step would catch dead code, duplicated utilities, and superseded implementations before they compound.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-16T18:34:44.339Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHPYJ2",
      "text": "Codex skill: handle own-PR reviews — GitHub rejects REQUEST_CHANGES on your own PRs, Codex should use COMMENT event instead. Bundle this fix with skill importing refinement so it propagates to all projects.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-17T23:21:55.357Z",
      "tags": [
        "codex",
        "skills"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHRTEV",
      "text": "Task-specific ephemeral AC: Support acceptance criteria directly on tasks (not just via spec_ref). Useful for implementation requirements, refactoring criteria, and one-off work that doesn't warrant a spec item. Task ACs would be checked during review but wouldn't live in the spec hierarchy. Addresses the gap where plan-imported ACs are behavioral specs vs task-level implementation requirements.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-18T16:48:43.957Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHRX2P",
      "text": "skill-render.ts lines 492, 730, 924 have LF-only frontmatter regexes. Low risk in render path (kspec generates these files with LF) but should be hardened for consistency with the CRLF fixes in skill.ts/validate-skills.ts.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-18T17:34:31.166Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHSJJR",
      "text": "Feature request: ralph loop boundary tracking in session logs. Currently no easy way to see what happened in a ralph loop iteration without cross-referencing PR timestamps, git log, and task states. A session log showing PR-to-task mapping per loop iteration would help audit and review. Originated from imgen project observation.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-18T23:50:17.810Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHV3EX",
      "text": "Design section configuration for agents generate — allow projects to control which sections appear (skills table, conventions, workflows, static templates). Key questions: where does config live, include vs exclude list, defaults, custom sections, ordering, data vs template distinction, migration path. See plan doc for full requirements.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T14:04:31.825Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "spec-gap"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHVCPE",
      "text": "Inbox tag management: no way to add/remove tags on existing inbox items. Only settable at creation via inbox add --tag. Need: kspec inbox tag add @ref <tag> and kspec inbox tag remove @ref <tag>.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T16:45:56.496Z",
      "tags": [
        "inbox",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHVCPE",
      "text": "Batch command arg naming inconsistency: inbox add accepts tag (singular) not tags. No documentation of which args each batch command accepts. Consider: consistent plural naming or better error messages with valid arg list.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T16:45:56.513Z",
      "tags": [
        "batch",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHVCPE",
      "text": "Stale workflow runs accumulate: no way to prune or auto-expire old runs. After many sessions, every workflow next command requires specifying a run ID because 7+ active runs exist. Need: kspec workflow prune (expire runs older than N days) or kspec workflow cancel @run-id.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T16:45:56.528Z",
      "tags": [
        "workflow",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHVE47",
      "text": "When spawning parallel review agents (e.g. Codex + /pr-review), instruct the /pr-review agent not to merge — only review. The parent agent should control the merge decision after all reviews complete. Update /pr-review skill or add a --no-merge flag.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T17:10:56.412Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHVQVV",
      "text": "Template/example repo for new kspec consumers: either a GitHub template repo or 'kspec create-project' command showing a fully configured consumer project (manifest, CLAUDE.md with @kspec-agents.md, skills, hooks). Real consumer projects (kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes) serve as informal examples but a clean minimal template would lower onboarding friction.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T20:01:07.957Z",
      "tags": [
        "dx",
        "external",
        "adoption"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHVR5K",
      "text": "Per-module task files and task archiving: Original design intent was project.tasks.yaml for non-spec tasks, <module>.tasks.yaml for module-scoped tasks. Never fully implemented — everything goes to project.tasks.yaml. Tradeoffs: splitting reduces file size (comfy-ecaj-nodes has 97 tasks in one file) but requires reading more files. Related: need task archiving to move completed tasks out of the active file. Both address the same scaling problem (task files growing unbounded) from different angles.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-19T20:06:26.877Z",
      "tags": [
        "design",
        "tasks",
        "scaling"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHWTXF",
      "text": "kspec validate @spec or @task — targeted validation that checks a single spec/task's AC coverage against codebase. Not full approval, just verifies each AC has at least one // AC: annotation in test files. Would make trait AC gaps immediately visible during task-work. Could be used by local-review skill as a concrete check instead of relying on agent diligence.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T06:13:40.815Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "spec-gap"
    },
