    {
      "ref": "01KHY9YB",
      "text": "Terminal exit code display in ralph CLI renderer — claude-agent-acp PR #316 adds _meta.terminal_exit.exit_code on Bash tool completions (opt-in via clientCapabilities._meta.terminal_output). Low priority, ~40 lines across events.ts + cli-renderer.ts. Only concrete gain from the terminal streaming protocol — the output data itself is identical to existing _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse path. Worth adopting if Bash failure debugging becomes a pain point.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T19:55:32.246Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYAGZ",
      "text": "Bash code fence language change in claude-agent-acp v0.18.0 — formatted Bash output changed from ```sh to ```console. Check if ralph's noise suppression patterns, session log rendering, or any regex patterns in cli-renderer.ts or events.ts match on the code fence language. Low risk since ralph primarily reads from _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse not content blocks, but worth a grep.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:05:43.175Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYAV7",
      "text": "Surface ACP usage/cost data in ralph session stats — after SDK bump to 0.14.x, new Usage/UsageUpdate/Cost types are available. Could add token usage per iteration and cumulative cost to session log stats and web UI. The usage_update SessionUpdate variant fires during sessions with context window utilization data.\n\n---\n\nIMPORTANT FINDING: Neither claude-agent-acp nor codex-acp actually emit usage_update events or populate PromptResponse.usage. Both have raw token data available but discard it. kynetic-bot works around this by scraping /context stderr (fragile regex). Upstream PR to claude-agent-acp is highest-value path — Anthropic API stream events contain usage data, just needs wiring to ACP protocol.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:11:19.317Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYDW5",
      "text": "Explore CLAUDE_CODE_SIMPLE mode for ralph loops — sets minimal system prompt with only Bash, file read, and file edit tools. Disables MCP tools, attachments, hooks, and CLAUDE.md. Could reduce token overhead and speed up startup, but ralph would need to inject all project context (AGENTS.md rules, spec-first workflow, kspec conventions) into the prompt itself instead of relying on Claude Code's built-in mechanisms. Tradeoff: simpler/faster agent vs ralph becomes responsible for all context bootstrapping. Ref: anthropics/claude-code#27019",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T21:04:14.935Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYFD9",
      "text": "Ralph worktree isolation for task work — spawn each agent in a git worktree under a gitignored .worktrees/ dir for branch isolation. Pattern proven in kynetic-internal with jj workspaces. Key insight: kspec resolves .kspec/ via git root, but worktrees return their own root from rev-parse --show-toplevel. Solution: ralph sets KSPEC_SPEC_DIR to point to main tree's .kspec/ when spawning agents (env var already exists for batch mode). Benefits: isolated branches per task, parallel agent work, trivial cleanup of failed work, clean main branch. Unknowns: shadow branch commands from worktree context, git config inheritance, worktree lifecycle management in ralph.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T21:31:05.321Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYTNN",
      "text": "Single-source task state diagram: currently duplicated in AGENTS.md, templates/agents-sections/03-task-lifecycle.md, and src/cli/help/content.ts. Adding needs_work required updating all three independently. Generate from schema or single template to avoid triple-update when adding states.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-21T00:47:53.828Z",
      "tags": [
        "reflection",
        "dx",
        "agents"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYTNN",
      "text": "Distinguish behavioral vs testable ACs in kspec validate: workflow ACs (agent behavioral specs enforced by skills/prompts) get flagged as uncovered in test coverage, creating false MUST-FIX findings in reviews. Allow tagging ACs or specs as agent-enforced to report separately from code-testable ACs.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-21T00:47:53.854Z",
      "tags": [
        "reflection",
        "validate",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KJ0K9C",
      "text": "inbox promote missing --slug option: cannot set task slug during promotion, must use default auto-generated slug. Add --slug <slug> option to inbox promote command.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-21T17:17:20.221Z",
