    },
    {
      "ref": "01KJ35CN",
      "text": "Plugin registry tests: validate structurally instead of exact output matching. Current tests assert exact JSON shapes (e.g. source field structure) which breaks when Claude Code schema evolves. Better: (1) Validate marketplace.json against a Zod schema capturing required fields (plugins array, name, source, version) rather than exact values. (2) Test build output structurally — 'has plugins array with our entry' not exact field matching. (3) For known_marketplaces.json registry, test entry exists with valid path, not exact source object shape. Motivation: the source field assertion broke twice already (local → directory object) because tests coupled to implementation details.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-22T17:12:10.776Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KJ43CP",
      "text": "Include triage records in static snapshot (kspec-snapshot.json). Currently the snapshot format (KspecSnapshot type) doesn't include triage records, so the triage page in static/GitHub Pages mode shows an empty state with a notice instead of displaying existing triage decisions read-only. AC-8 of @interactive-triage-ui expects read-only display. Needs: add triage records to export snapshot, update KspecSnapshot type, add fetchTriageRecordsStatic to read from snapshot.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-23T01:56:29.205Z",
