    {
      "ref": "01KJ77S4",
      "text": "Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging on stdin), ralph has no mechanism to detect or recover. A configurable per-iteration timeout (e.g., 15-20 min) that kills the stuck agent and logs the failure would prevent indefinite hangs. Separate from Claude Code's per-bash-command timeout which didn't prevent the kspec batch stdin hang.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-24T07:10:54.335Z",
