      "text": "kspec setup should work without CLAUDECODE=1 env var in non-interactive contexts. Either add a --agent flag (e.g. kspec setup --agent claude-code) to explicitly specify the agent type, or detect based on installed tooling (~/.claude exists) rather than requiring runtime env vars. Discovered while building containerized ralph runner — entrypoint bash script can't set CLAUDECODE=1 globally because claude blocks nested sessions.",
